page RecipeRenderFromNode(path: "/recipes/render-from-node", title: "Render templates from Node — Recipes", description: "The Node binding is a small wrapper around `wf render`.") {
    RecipeShell("Render templates from Node", summary: "The Node binding is a small wrapper around `wf render`. Install it with npm:  ```bash npm install webfluent ```  The binding needs `wf` itself installed. It looks for it at `WF_BIN`, then on `PATH`, then in `~/.webfluent/bin` and `~/.cargo/bin` (and, outside Windows, `/usr/local/bin` and `/usr/bin`). Its version is the compiler's.  This Express app renders an invoice as HTML and as a PDF:  ```js const \{ Template \} = require(\"webfluent\");  const templates = Template.fromDir(\"templates\");          // or fromFile, fromString const invoice = templates.page(\"Invoice\");  app.get(\"/invoices/:id\", async (req, res) => \{ const data = await loadInvoice(req.params.id); res.send(await invoice.renderHtmlAsync(data)); \}); app.get(\"/invoices/:id.pdf\", async (req, res) => \{ res.type(\"application/pdf\").send(await invoice.renderPdfAsync(await loadInvoice(req.params.id))); \}); ```  Every render has a synchronous form (`renderHtml`, `renderHtmlFragment`, `renderPdf`, `renderSlides`) and an `…Async` form that does not block the event loop. Use the `…Async` forms in a server. `withTheme`, `withTokens` and `withLang` set what the Rust API sets.  A render runs `wf` once and takes a few milliseconds. The data goes over standard input, so nothing is written to disk.", outputs: [], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Call WF from a script", to: "/recipes/call-wf-from-a-script"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Call your own JavaScript", to: "/recipes/call-your-own-script"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Draw a chart from a library", to: "/recipes/chart-from-a-library")], source: "md-docs/recipes/render-from-node.md", how: false, hasVariations: false) {
    }
}
